  "solution": "The pattern followed here is:\n\n**Logic: (First number × Second number) × 4 = Third number.**\n\n1) (6, 17, 408)\n\n⇒ (6 × 17) × 4\n\n⇒ 102 × 4 = 408\n\n2) (13, 27, 1404)\n\n⇒ (13 × 27) × 4\n\n⇒ 351 × 4 = 1404\n\nLet's check each option one by one:\n\n**Option 1) **(9, 27, 245)\n\n⇒ (9 × 27) × 4\n\n⇒ 243 × 4 = 972 ≠ 245. (Incorrect)\n\n**Option 2) **(17, 28, 952)\n\n⇒ (17 × 28) × 4\n\n⇒ 476 × 4 = 1904 ≠ 952. (Incorrect)\n\n**Option 3) **(5, 82, 1200)\n\n⇒ (5 × 82) × 4\n\n⇒ 410 × 4 = 1640 ≠ 1200. (Incorrect)\n\n**Option 4) **(4, 26, 416)\n\n⇒ (4 × 26) × 4\n\n⇒ 104 × 4 = 416 = 416 (Correct)\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(4, 26, 416)\".**",
